## Applied service-boundary cut

The implementation cut is complete at the service/type boundary and deliberately incomplete at the physical module boundary:

| Surface | Public callables | Applied rule |
|---|---:|---|
| `RuntimeKernelService` | 36 | Stateless constructor plus the exact 35 `Retain trusted core` methods. |
| `runtime::RuntimeOwnerServices` | 110 | Constructor, 84 non-constructor compatibility delegates, and 25 non-effect owner extractions. |
| `runtime::RuntimeProjectionService` | 44 | Constructor plus the exact 43 projection/read methods. |
| `kernel::RuntimeEffectCompatibilityGateway` | 9 | Constructor plus eight effectful methods whose complete authority-and-receipt path is not yet proven. |
| Retired | 2 | `evaluate_coding_tool_budget_policy` and `issue_capability_lease` are absent from all four surfaces. |

The effect compatibility residual is exactly `invoke_model_mount_provider`, `invoke_model_mount_provider_stream`, `supervise_model_mount_backend_process`, `run_coding_tool_step_module`, `execute_private_workspace_ctee_action`, `apply_workspace_restore_operations`, `capture_workspace_snapshot_files`, and `apply_workspace_snapshot_restore`. Their placement is not a completed owner extraction claim. Each remains blocked on proof of pre-effect owner/authority admission, zero effect on denial, exact observed-effect receipt binding, and replay/crash behavior.

Physical namespace shrink is also not complete. The current `runtime/kernel/` tree has 134 Rust files and 76 root public modules. Fifty-two root delegate modules touched by non-trusted baseline rows remain under that namespace; four (`approval`, `ctee`, `model_mount`, and `projection`) mix trusted and non-trusted responsibilities and require splitting before safe relocation. [`runtime-kernel-namespace-residual.v1.json`](./runtime-kernel-namespace-residual.v1.json) is the exact machine-verified residual ledger.

